{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.AdelicSubstrate","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.AdelicSubstrate","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.AdelicSubstrate.nonArchimedean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.AdelicSubstrate.nonArchimedean","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/adelic-substrate.lean#L32-L32","doc":"Non-archimedean projection π_p : A → Loc p at each prime p. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.AdelicSubstrate.archimedean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.AdelicSubstrate.archimedean","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/adelic-substrate.lean#L30-L30","doc":"Archimedean projection π_∞ : A → ℝ (the laboratory continuum). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.AdelicSubstrate.Loc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.AdelicSubstrate.Loc","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/adelic-substrate.lean#L28-L28","doc":"Local non-archimedean rings, indexed by rational primes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.AdelicSubstrate.Carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.AdelicSubstrate.Carrier","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/adelic-substrate.lean#L26-L26","doc":"The carrier ring of the substrate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.AdelicSubstrate.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.AdelicSubstrate.mk","kind":"ctor","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/adelic-substrate.lean#L24-L24","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.AdelicSubstrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.AdelicSubstrate","kind":"structure","line":12,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/adelic-substrate.lean#L12-L32","doc":"The **adelic substrate** of the QOU framework.\n\nAbstract interface: a ring `A` carrying an archimedean place\n(projection to `ℝ`) and a non-archimedean place per rational\nprime `p` (projection to a local quantum-state ring `Loc p`),\ntogether with the restricted-product compatibility of the\nrational adele ring `𝔸_ℚ = ℝ × ∏'_p ℚ_p`.\n\nThe QOU instance identifies each `Loc p` with the localized\nquantum-geometric state at the `p`-th cyclotomic / Kummer\nlevel of the Habiro completion, and the archimedean projection\nwith the classical-limit functor on the substrate. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:adelic-substrate","label":"def:adelic-substrate","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/adelic-substrate.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}